      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While over-the-counter pain relievers might help with muscle soreness, self-treating symptoms suggestive of DVT is risky. Ibuprofen and aspirin are not substitutes for a medical diagnosis, especially when concerning symptoms like leg pain are present after long travel. Given your worries, I strongly encourage you to call your GP or a telehealth service for advice rather than waiting or self-medicating. They can offer guidance over the phone before you decide on an urgent visit.",
      "source": "target",
